## Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js (App Router) project with Payload CMS.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using pnpm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` with the new package and its dependencies

#### 2. Frontend Layout Integration
- Modified `src/app/(frontend)/layout.tsx` to integrate analytics
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the main content
- This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router

### Implementation Details

The integration follows the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (fetched on 2026-08-29):
- Used the Next.js App Router specific integration method
- The Analytics component was added to the frontend layout (not the Payload admin layout) to track visitor activity on the public-facing pages
- The component is placed at the end of the body tag as recommended by Vercel

### Files Modified

1. **package.json** - Added `@vercel/analytics` dependency
2. **pnpm-lock.yaml** - Updated with new package dependencies  
3. **src/app/(frontend)/layout.tsx** - Added Analytics component

### Verification

✓ **Build**: Successfully compiled with no errors using `pnpm run build`
✓ **Type Check**: TypeScript compilation passed with no errors using `pnpm run type-check`
✓ **Dependencies**: Lock file properly updated with all transitive dependencies

### Notes

- The Analytics component was added to the frontend layout only (not the Payload admin layout)
- The ESLint configuration has a pre-existing issue unrelated to these changes
- Once deployed to Vercel, analytics will automatically start collecting data
- To view analytics data, enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
- The analytics script will only load in production deployments on Vercel

### Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel (via `vercel deploy` or Git integration)
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Analytics → Enable)
3. After deployment, verify analytics are working by checking the Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. View collected data in the Vercel dashboard after a few days of traffic
